# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merged with sight-cpp/.gitignore when the sight-cpp / backend-python split was
# dissolved (see docs/architecture/DIRECTORY_ORDERING.md). Every path in that
# file was already relative to sight-cpp's root, so promoting it left the paths
# correct untouched — itself a small sign the split was never structural.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python virtualenv. Machine-specific and never portable between checkouts —
# it was carrying 827 tracked files.
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent worktrees (git already keeps their metadata; the trees are disposable).
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-user agent permission grants. .claude/settings.json IS committed — it
# carries the project-wide deny rules that keep tooling out of the vendored and
# generated trees — but settings.local.json accumulates one-off allows specific
# to one machine's paths and shell history.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. All of this was TRACKED — 1,296 files, 592 MB, including a
# 70 MB .dSYM DWARF blob and a 14.6 MB precompiled header. Object files are
# machine- and flag-specific: committing them means every rebuild dirties the
# tree, every pull can hand you objects compiled against different headers,
# and `git status` is too noisy to read. None of it belongs in history.
#
# Untracking does NOT delete anything on disk, and does not change the build:
# the Makefile regenerates all of it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
*.o
*.d
*.gch
*.dSYM/
# The default clang output name, left behind by one-off `c++ foo.cpp` probes.
a.out

# Linked binaries: the app, the tools, and every test executable. `make test`
# deletes and relinks these on every run by design (a leftover binary from a
# failed build is a stale binary waiting to be trusted), so tracking them
# guarantees a permanently dirty tree.
/earthcall
/migrate_saves
/read_laws
/*_test

# Build log output — generated logs from compilation sessions.
build_logs/
# Binaries that got built next to their sources rather than at the root.
src/earthcall
tests/*_test

# Instrumented objects from `make asan-test`. Deliberately a separate tree from
# build/ so ASan objects can never be linked into an ordinary binary — and not
# committed, because it is a full second copy of every object file.
build-asan/

# WebAssembly build output — the same problem as build/ above, missed the
# first time. fc25329 committed 81 files here (a 4.1 MB earthcall.wasm, a
# 12.8 MB compiler_depend.make, a CMakeCache.txt pinned to one machine's
# emsdk path); e5d3fc5 then deleted ~267k lines of it again. A fresh clone
# inherits the stale CMakeCache and fails to configure until this directory
# is deleted by hand. Regenerates from `cmake -S . -B build-wasm ...`.
#
# NOTE: build-wasm/index.html is, as of this writing, the only page that
# boots the wasm build (it sets Module.canvas to the #earthcall-canvas
# selector WebGpuContext_wasm.cpp hardcodes) and is currently tracked despite
# living in this directory. It should move to a tracked, non-ignored home
# (e.g. web_ui/) before `rm -rf build-wasm` is allowed to destroy it again —
# see docs/WASM_FIX_NOTES.md.
build-wasm/

# node_modules, wherever it lands (e.g. scratch/experiments/puppeteer_test/node_modules,
# 2,221 files committed by the same fc25329 above). Regenerates via `npm
# install`.
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rest of the build trees. `build/` above was ignored; these were not, and
# they were TRACKED — 2,219 files across build2/, build_ag/ and build_agy/
# (CMakeFiles/ scaffolding plus fully-expanded _deps/ checkouts of asio,
# flatbuffers, glfw, vhacd and websocketpp). Same objection as build/: machine-
# and flag-specific, regenerated by cmake, and each one is a second and third
# copy of every dependency's source tree for any tool that walks the repo.
#
# The cmake-build-* names are what CLion generates by default; they appear
# whenever the project is configured from the IDE rather than the shell.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build2/
build_ag/
build_agy/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# clangd's index cache (see AGENTS.md "clangd"). Regenerated from
# build/compile_commands.json on the next `clangd --check` or editor open, and
# rewritten on nearly every keystroke/reindex — 582 tracked .idx files were
# dirtying `git status` on every session with no diff worth reviewing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored dependency SOURCE. This is deliberately ignored but still TRACKED:
# CLAUDE.md's build recipe points OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR at local_deps/openssl-3.0.13
# and there is no system OpenSSL to fall back on, so a fresh clone must still
# receive these files — `git rm --cached` here would break the build for anyone
# else. Listing them here does not untrack them; it only takes them out of the
# walk that ripgrep, fd and every editor's fuzzy-finder perform.
#
# The motivation is scale, not tidiness: 13,324 of this repository's 17,134
# tracked files live under local_deps/ — 78% of the tree — against roughly 330
# .cpp/.hpp files of actual Earthcall source. Every project-wide search was
# paying for OpenSSL's test suite and perlasm generators before it reached
# src/. Modifications to tracked files still show in `git status` as normal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local_deps/
third_party/asio/
third_party/flatbuffers/
third_party/glfw/
third_party/websocketpp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Saved worlds. These are runtime output, not source: 706 files totalling
# 2.0 GB, with individual saves reaching 98 MB of single-line JSON. Nothing
# reads them except the loader, and no tool that opens files by size survives
# one by accident.
#
# Only saves/games/ is ignored. saves/fixtures/, saves/avatars/ and
# saves/integrations/ hold small, hand-authored seeds that tests and docs refer
# to (test_avatar.ecsave, web_apps.ecsave, inference_law.json …); they belong in
# history. An earlier draft of this block used a blanket `*.ecsave`, which
# silently took those three directories with it — hence the narrow path here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
saves/games/

# The law audit trail (LawAuditLogger). Regenerated every run, and at Verbose
# it grows fast enough that committing it would be its own problem.
/logs/
saves/earthcall-io.log

# wgpu-native: we static-link the .a (committed); the .dylib is unused.
third_party/wgpu/lib/libwgpu_native.dylib
webgpu_smoke
webgpu_mesh
webgpu_renderer
webgpu_window

# JetBrains per-user workspace state.
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identity key material. A Person's private key IS that Person: anyone holding
# it can sign as them, and unlike a password there is nothing to rotate on the
# far side — every claim they ever signed becomes forgeable.
#
# The KeyStore writes outside the repo by default ($EARTHCALL_HOME, else
# ~/.earthcall/identity). Everything below is defence in depth for the case
# where someone points it at the working tree, or drops a key beside a save
# while debugging. It costs nothing and the failure it prevents is permanent:
# a key pushed to GitHub is compromised the moment it lands, and rewriting
# history does not un-publish it.
#
# NOTE ON SIGNATURES: signatures inside save files are deliberately NOT ignored.
# A signature is public by construction — it is what lets a loader verify a
# claim without holding any secret — and stripping it from a committed save
# would make that save unverifiable, which is the opposite of the goal. Only
# standalone secret material and detached attestation sidecars are excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.earthcall/
earthcall_home/

# Private keys and seeds, by extension and by conventional name.
*.key
*.seed
*.pem
*.p8
*.pfx
*.p12
id_ed25519*
*_private.json
*.privkey

# Whole key directories, wherever they land.
keys/
identity/keys/
**/identity/private/
secrets/

# Detached attestation sidecars (the signature inside a save file stays).
*.attestation
*.sig

# Environment files: EARTHCALL_CLOUD_TOKEN and friends live here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
